\begin{abstract}
We prove that for all integers $k \geq 1$, there exists a constant $C_k$ depending only on $k$ such that for all $q > C_k$ and for all $n \geq 1$ every matrix in $M_n(\F_q)$ is a sum of two $k$th powers.
\end{abstract}
\keywords{Waring problem, Lang-Weil estimate,  finite fields.}
